<BaseLayout
  title="Refund Policy — Rosetta Q"
  description="When we refund in full, and why the result of a measurement is never grounds for a refund."
  lang="en"
  altUrl="/es/reembolsos/"
  pageCss={css}>
  <article class="article wrap legal">
      <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
      <p><strong>Rosetta Quantum</strong> is a brand of <strong>Blue Tuna SpA</strong> (Chile). Payments are handled by <strong>Paddle.com</strong>, which acts as Merchant of Record: Paddle is the seller of record for your purchase, runs the checkout, issues the invoice, handles taxes/VAT, and processes refunds. Paddle's buyer terms apply to the purchase itself.</p>
      <h2>1. The principle: you pay for the measurement, not for the verdict</h2>
      <p>What we sell is a sealed, verifiable <strong>measurement</strong>, not a favorable outcome. We never promise specific results, performance, or business outcomes — and results can be negative.</p>
      <p>A <strong>negative result is a complete, valid deliverable</strong>. It is measured, sealed, and reported with the same care as a positive one, and it is charged the same way. A negative result does not by itself void or discount your invoice.</p>
      <p>The refund right described below applies to every paid product <strong>regardless of whether your result was positive or negative</strong> — that is the point: the refund is about your purchase, not about the verdict.</p>
      <p>Our deliverables are measurements, not advice. Nothing we deliver constitutes medical, financial, or investment advice.</p>
      <h2>2. Full refund, no questions asked</h2>
      <p>For every <strong>one-off paid product</strong>, you can request a <strong>full refund, no questions asked, within 14 days of delivery of your deliverable</strong>. For the <strong>Monitor</strong> subscription, see section 3.</p>
      <ul><li>You do not need to give a reason.</li><li>The refund is for the full amount you paid.</li><li>Products listed as free at <a href="https://rosettaquantum.com/pricing/">rosettaquantum.com/pricing/</a> involve no payment, so there is nothing to refund.</li></ul>
      <p>Current products and prices are published at <a href="https://rosettaquantum.com/pricing/">rosettaquantum.com/pricing/</a>.</p>
      <h2>3. Monitor subscription</h2>
      <p><strong>Monitor</strong> is a monthly subscription.</p>
      <ul><li>You can <strong>cancel anytime</strong>. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period; you keep access until then.</li><li><strong>Only your first charge is refundable</strong> — in full, within 14 days of that charge, no questions asked. Later charges are not refundable under this policy; instead, you can cancel at any time.</li><li>If you have questions or need help with cancellation, contact us at <strong><a href="mailto:hello@rosettaquantum.com">hello@rosettaquantum.com</a></strong> with the order reference from your Paddle receipt.</li></ul>
      <h2>4. How to request a refund</h2>
      <p>1. Email <strong><a href="mailto:hello@rosettaquantum.com">hello@rosettaquantum.com</a></strong> with the <strong>order reference from your Paddle receipt</strong>.<br>2. That's it — no justification needed.</p>
      <p>Refunds are processed by <strong>Paddle</strong> to the <strong>original payment method</strong> used for the purchase.</p>
      <h2>5. Your statutory rights</h2>
      <p>This policy adds to — and does not limit or replace — any rights you have as a consumer under applicable law. Our relationship with you is governed by the law of <strong>Chile</strong>. Paddle's buyer terms apply to the purchase transaction itself.</p>
      <h2>6. Contact</h2>
      <p><strong>Blue Tuna SpA</strong> (brand: Rosetta Quantum)<br>Email: <strong><a href="mailto:hello@rosettaquantum.com">hello@rosettaquantum.com</a></strong></p>

      <p class="sello-fuente">Published from its approved source document ·
        <code>sha256:7323b77f2f6f7ab9…</code></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
